{"slug":"richard-neal","qid":"Q1464697","name":"Richard Neal","desc":"American politician (born 1949)","article":"Richard Neal","born":"1949-02-14","died":null,"birthplace":"Springfield","parties":["Democratic Party"],"offices":[{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"MA-01","f":2013,"u":null},{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"MA-02","f":1989,"u":2013}],"summary":"Richard Edmund Neal (born February 14, 1949) is an American politician serving as the U.S. representative for Massachusetts's 1st congressional district since 1989. The district, numbered as the 2nd district from 1989 to 2013, includes Springfield, West Springfield, Pittsfield, Holyoke, Agawam, Chicopee, and Westfield. A member of the Democratic Party, Neal has been the dean of Massachusetts's delegation to the United States House of Representatives since 2013, and is dean of the New England House delegations.","photo":{"f":"richard-neal.jpg","by":"US House Office of Photography","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":null,"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Richard_Neal_official_photo_(cropped).jpg"},"history":[{"y":2026,"o":"H","k":"MA-01","p":"D","n":"Richard Neal","race":"MA-01"},{"y":2024,"o":"H","k":"MA-01","p":"D","v":223325,"s":62.37,"w":true,"n":"Richard E. Neal"},{"y":2022,"o":"H","k":"MA-01","p":"D","v":157635,"s":61.48,"w":true,"n":"Richard E Neal"},{"y":2020,"o":"H","k":"MA-01","p":"D","v":275376,"s":96.51,"w":true,"n":"Richard E Neal"},{"y":2018,"o":"H","k":"MA-01","p":"D","v":211790,"s":97.64,"w":true,"n":"Richard E Neal"},{"y":2016,"o":"H","k":"MA-01","p":"D","v":235803,"s":73.34,"w":true,"n":"Richard E Neal"},{"y":2014,"o":"H","k":"MA-01","p":"D","v":167612,"s":97.96,"w":true,"n":"Richard E Neal"},{"y":2012,"o":"H","k":"MA-01","p":"D","v":261936,"s":98.42,"w":true,"n":"Richard E Neal"},{"y":2010,"o":"H","k":"MA-02","p":"D","v":122751,"s":57.33,"w":true,"n":"Richard E Neal"},{"y":2008,"o":"H","k":"MA-02","p":"D","v":234369,"s":98.47,"w":true,"n":"Richard E Neal"},{"y":2006,"o":"H","k":"MA-02","p"